lock-group tool-section tool-benefits\"><!-- wp:heading {\"level\":2} --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">What it does</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->\n<!-- wp:list --><ul class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Convert supported image formats to JPEG.</li><!-- /wp:list-item -->\n<!-- wp:list-item --><li>Aim for a configurable file-size target.</li><!-- /wp:list-item -->\n<!-- wp:list-item --><li>Preserve folder structure in a fresh output tree.</li><!-- /wp:list-item -->\n</ul><!-- /wp:list -->\n</div><!-- /wp:group -->\n<!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"tool-section tool-requirements\"} --><div class=\"wp-block-group tool-section tool-requirements\"><!-- wp:heading {\"level\":2} --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Requirements</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>64-bit Windows 10/11; Windows PowerShell 5.1 or PowerShell 7; ImageMagick 7.1.2-32 or a newer supported 7.x build on PATH. Windows 10 is documented but untested; decoding depends on the installed build.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n</div><!-- /wp:group -->\n<!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"tool-section tool-start\"} --><div class=\"wp-block-group tool-section tool-start\"><!-- wp:heading {\"level\":2} --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Get started</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Extract the package, install ImageMagick, then drag one folder onto <code>WinImgNormalizer.bat</code>. Output goes into a new Windows Pictures folder.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n</div><!-- /wp:group -->\n<!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"tool-section tool-limits\"} --><div class=\"wp-block-group tool-section tool-limits\"><!-- wp:heading {\"level\":2} --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Output & limits</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Default target is 1,048,576 bytes (1 MiB), best effort. Above-target results can carry warnings. Images become sRGB JPEGs on white, with metadata removed; videos retain original bytes/metadata. Animation and multipage images produce one selected frame/page. Duplicate skipping is heuristic, not content-hash verification.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n</div><!-- /wp:group -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"tool-return\"} --><p class=\"tool-return\"><a href=\"{{page:home}}#tools\">&larr; Back to all tools</a></p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n",
