hat it does</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->\n<!-- wp:list --><ul class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Convert MP3, M4A and OGG audio in batches.</li><!-- /wp:list-item -->\n<!-- wp:list-item --><li>Use 64 kbps CBR by default, or choose another bitrate.</li><!-- /wp:list-item -->\n<!-- wp:list-item --><li>Add optional cover art and shared artist/album tags.</li><!-- /wp:list-item -->\n</ul><!-- /wp:list -->\n</div><!-- /wp:group -->\n<!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"tool-section tool-requirements\"} --><div class=\"wp-block-group tool-section tool-requirements\"><!-- wp:heading {\"level\":2} --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Requirements</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Windows 11; Windows PowerShell or PowerShell 7; FFmpeg and FFprobe beside the script or on PATH. Exact minimum dependency versions remain to be confirmed for v1.0.0.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n</div><!-- /wp:group -->\n<!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"tool-section tool-start\"} --><div class=\"wp-block-group tool-section tool-start\"><!-- wp:heading {\"level\":2} --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Get started</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Extract the final release, supply dependencies, and drag a source folder onto <code>AudioFileForPhone.bat</code>.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n</div><!-- /wp:group -->\n<!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"tool-section tool-limits\"} --><div class=\"wp-block-group tool-section tool-limits\"><!-- wp:heading {\"level\":2} --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Output & limits</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>New MP3 tree under Windows Music, mirrored subfolders, date-prefixed shortened filenames, collision suffixes and a run log. OGG supports Vorbis/Opus; <code>.opus</code>, WAV and FLAC are not scanned by the current documented workflow. MP3 conversion is lossy. Filename sanitizing does not establish compatibility with every phone/player. This is conversion, not the speech-cleaning workflow of WinAudioClean.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n</div><!-- /wp:group -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"tool-return\"} --><p class=\"tool-return\"><a href=\"{{page:home}}#tools\">&larr; Back to all tools</a></p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n",
